    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec: on `POST /api/owners`, when no `registrationDate` is supplied, default it to the server's current date; the field round-trips back through `GET` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes (minimal, low structural impact):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The generator maps `format: date` \u2192 `LocalDate`, so both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) get the field automatically, and MapStruct maps it by name in both directions with no mapper edits.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) column with a getter/setter, so it persists and survives the create\u2192read round trip.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the single existing create step now defaults the date in place: `if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());`. Folding the default into this one-method class avoided adding a new pipeline function *and* a new YAML step.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to all four `schema.sql` files. Only `hsqldb` (the test profile) used positional seed inserts, so I appended a `NULL` to its 10 `owners` rows; h2/postgres/mysql use explicit column lists and needed no data edits.\n\nI kept the touched functions simple: `BuildOwner` gained one branch in a single-method class (WMC_other = 0), and the entity only received a trivial getter/setter pair rather than growing any existing method.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite are green.",
